    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d163">

                <pb facs="0271" n="259" xml:id="pg259"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/4999a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-03-23T14:00:00-05:00">March 23, 1937—2 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>98. We understand that British military officers are now in Spain observing the
                    military activities of the insurgent forces. We would like to know for our
                    confidential information what arrangements may have been made to permit British
                    officers to act in this manner in territory occupied by the insurgents as we
                    understand that up to the present the British Government has not granted status
                    of belligerency to the insurgents. Please furnish all details available.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
